 "heard": "Your dollar is named after a deer! 1748. A traitor slides a barrel across the counter. Not coins. Not paper. Deer skins. Out here, nobody had money. But everybody had deer. One good skin bought you a knife. Five bought you a barrel. Then a man writes in his journal that he was robbed of 300 bucks. Not dollars. The US dollar didn't exist yet. It showed up 44 years later. in 1792. By then, people already had a word for \"one unit of stuff you trade.\" So that's probably why your dollar is a buck. Historians still argue about it. Me? I just like the name."
}
